title Arc two -- two rooms, a closed door, and a declined name
prompt open arc two
think Read arc two as the survey scoped it and found two of its four items already landed. counsel folded and the remaining dated rooms folded in the two rounds before this one, so what was left was the room split, the counsel close, and the journal decline recorded rather than merely deferred.
think Opened active-development as the sibling rather than as a replacement, because the diagnosis was never that active-designing was wrong -- it was that two tempos were sharing one shelf and the numerous one was crowding the durable one.
think Kept the placement test to one blunt question. A filing rule that needs a paragraph of adjudication gets skipped, and a skipped rule is exactly how one room came to hold two kinds of writing in the first place.
think Refused the retroactive re-sort and said so in the room's own README. The 629 notes that folded out of active-designing stay where they are; a week spent re-sorting would make old files feel tidier without making one of them truer. The test governs what is born forward.
think Bounded the new room from birth rather than letting it earn enforcement later by folding. The seat is earned by folding because a folded room has proven its references survive the move -- yet a room born under the law never accumulated a backlog, so there is nothing to grandfather and nothing to prove. That is a second, honest way onto the roster, and the scan says so in its own comment.
think Wrote the counsel banner to say closed rather than retired, and made the distinction load-bearing: 764 pieces stand as filed, 1,977 references point in, and every one still resolves. Closed means no longer growing, never no longer true.
think Held the line on mining counsel wholesale, which the survey already argued and this round did not reopen. Reading 764 files to extract insight is a project measured in weeks with an unknowable yield; it stalls, and a half-converted room is worse than either end. On touch, then, and only then.
think Recorded the journal decline in three places rather than dropping it, because a question answered only in conversation is a question that gets asked again. Dimeroll owns the word as a book of record and the Lexicon already assigns it to the logs -- session-logs IS the journal, and a third home would braid one word across three meanings.
obs The roster-size assert earned its keep within minutes of being written. Adding active-development moved enforced_rooms_named_absent from 5 to 6 and the witness reddened at once. That number is the roster size on purpose: a room joining or leaving is a seated decision and should have to be written down rather than sliding in unremarked.
obs active-designing reads 2 flat rather than 0 for the same reason it did last round -- 33 day-only names that no instrument counts. Naming that again here rather than fixing it quietly inside a room-split, since it is still its own word.
obs The living-docs lint advisories that mention active-designing name files now in yonder and predate this round; nothing new was orphaned by opening a room.
loom rooms=enforce_roster enforced=6 advised=12 enforced_over=0 advised_over=0 bound=256
loom rooms=new active_development_flat=0 counsel_flat=0 counsel_dated_pieces=764 counsel_inbound_refs=1977
loom census=unchanged refs_lost=193 lost_ceiling=193 under_ceiling=yes
file active-development/README.md the new room -- what it holds, the one test, and what deliberately does not move
file .claude/rules/design-rooms.md the law -- one question, the counsel close, the journal decline
file .cursor/rules/design-rooms.mdc the Cursor twin
file counsel/README.md the closed banner, accreted above the body rather than rewriting it
file active-designing/README.md the boundary named at its own front door, pointing next door
file ORGANIZING.md the new room filed beside its siblings in the shape of the tree
file CLAUDE.md the context-home list carries both rooms and the test
file context/LEXICON.md three rows -- active-development, closed room, journal declined
file tools/fixtures/room_bound_scan.sh six enforced; born-under-the-law named as the second way onto the roster
file tools/room_bound_witness.rish active-development asserted by name; the roster-size pin moved 5 to 6
recommend check-in (checkpoint) arc two is closed and the tree stands folded, bounded, enforced, and filed. Two doors from the survey remain unopened and both want a word rather than a kg -- the color normalization booked as REDS %114, which edits dated bodies, and arc four's first-hour tutorial with the README metrics block, which is gated on REDS %112, the fascia meter that still cannot report. Arc three, the vocabulary pruning, is the largest remaining piece and is a word of its own.
